</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Watermarks in EDMs are Radioactive.</span>

For <span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Recipe</span> which adds the watermarks directly to the images, the watermark detection rate is <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100\%</annotation></semantics></math> in the watermarked original training data <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. This data is then used to train <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. We find that the watermark successfully transfers from the output of EDM <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to EDM <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (see the first row in <a href="#S5.T1" title="In 5.2 Analyzing Watermark Radioactivity ‣ 5 Empirical Evaluation ‣ Radioactive Watermarks in Diffusion and AutoregressiveImage Generative Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). This aligns with expectations: when a watermark is present in the training data and propagates to the output of <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, it should, by transitivity, implicitly transfer to the output of <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> as well, given that both models perform the same task. The EDM architecture facilitates this transfer, as images are directly generated and learned in the image space. This direct reconstruction of pixel values, without abstraction into the latent space, enhances the retention of watermarks.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S5.T2.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S5.T2.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:129%;">Extensive fine-tuning on a single watermarked sample does not enforce watermark transfer in LDMs.<span id="S5.T2.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Given the observed lack of watermark transferability in LDMs, we extend our analysis from <a href="#S5.T1" title="In 5.2 Analyzing Watermark Radioactivity ‣ 5 Empirical Evaluation ‣ Radioactive Watermarks in Diffusion and AutoregressiveImage Generative Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> to an extreme scenario aimed at transferring a specific watermark instance. We use the metrics from <a href="#S5.T1" title="In 5.2 Analyzing Watermark Radioactivity ‣ 5 Empirical Evaluation ‣ Radioactive Watermarks in Diffusion and AutoregressiveImage Generative Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Additionally, we observe that neither the Tree-Ring watermark transfer from LDMs to RAR-B nor WIAR transfers to LDMs.

</span></span></figcaption>
<table id="S5.T2.10" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
